_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 7
---
order: 7
---
short_label: II.7
---
statement: If a straight line is cut at random, then the sum of the square on the whole and that on one of the segments equals twice the rectangle contained by the whole and the said segment plus the square on the remaining segment.
---
proof:

Let a straight line *AB* be cut at random at the point *C.*

I say that the sum of the squares on *AB* and *BC* equals twice the rectangle *AB* by *BC* plus the square on *CA.*

<figure class="diagram">
